    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "In StateFlow, each state is associated with a set of <strong>output functions</strong> that are executed when the state is entered. These functions can include calling an LLM with a specific instruction, executing a tool or environment, or generating a prompt. The next state is determined by the <strong>state transition function</strong>, which takes into account the current state and context history.",
